      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-induced local lattice strain creates regions of enhanced magnetocrystalline anisotropy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The distorted, higher-anisotropy regions act as pinning centers for magnetic domain walls.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Domain-wall pinning hinders wall motion and thereby increases the coercive field.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon-doped FeCoNi will maintain high saturation magnetization while exhibiting greater coercivity.",
